  * Boot arg negroniadreno=N performs steps 1..N (default 0: nothing).
  *   1  reads   GCC branches that feed the GPU (CFG AHB, MEMNOC GFX, SNOC DVM, DDRSS GPU AXI)
  *   2  reads   GPUCC: CX/GX GDSC state and the CX-side clocks, only when CFG AHB runs
- *   3  reads   GMU CX registers (needs CX GDSC on and the GMU clock): AO counter, GMU state
+ *   3  reads   GMU CX registers, only if CX and the GMU clock are already on
+ *   4  writes  the CX GDSC on (clears SW_COLLAPSE, waits for PWR_ON)
+ *   5  writes  GCC: GPLL0 GPU taps voted, MEMNOC/SNOC DVM/DDRSS GPU AXI on;
+ *              GPUCC: GMU clock 200 MHz and hub 150 MHz from the GPLL0 300 MHz tap,
+ *              then the CX clocks (AHB, CXO, hub AON, hub CX int, CX GMU, SMMU vote)
+ *   6  reads   the GMU's first words: the always-on counter must count
+ * negroniadreno_pause=MS waits after each announcement (default 500), so the
+ * persistent log has the line before a silent reset.
  *
  * Addresses: sm8450.dtsi (gpu@3d00000, gmu@3d6a000, gpucc@3d90000,
- * gcc@100000); offsets: Linux gcc-sm8450.c, gpucc-sm8450.c, a6xx_gmu.xml.
+ * gcc@100000); offsets: Linux gcc-sm8450.c, gpucc-sm8450.c, gdsc.c,
+ * clk-rcg2.c, a6xx_gmu.xml. The GPU block is left powered when the ladder
+ * ends (nothing else uses it yet).
  */
